From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:30:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Don't send WM_MOUSELEAVE to the window
 holding the mouse capture.

For TrackMouseEvent the window the mouse is in is the window that gets
the mouse messages, which while the mouse is captured is the capture
window, client area, wherever the pointer is. Windows (and ReactOS, which
mirrors it) therefore sends the leave only after the capture is released.
get_mouse_window() looked up the window under the cursor instead, so a
captured drag that crossed the window's edge got WM_MOUSELEAVE mid-drag
and, for example, a scroll bar thumb stopped following the pointer.

The capture check comes before the check for the pointer being over
another application's window, which applies once the capture is gone.

From neutron-wine (Nico-LaFoucate).
---
 dlls/win32u/input.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
index d4bd41b..203673f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1836,9 +1836,18 @@ static void check_mouse_leave( HWND hwnd, int hittest, struct mouse_tracking_inf
 static HWND get_mouse_window( HWND hwnd, INT *hittest, POINT *ret_pos, struct mouse_tracking_info *tracking )
 {
     POINT pos;
-    HWND ret;
+    HWND ret, capture;
 
     NtUserGetCursorPos( &pos );
+    /* while the mouse is captured, the capture window gets the mouse messages wherever
+     * the pointer is, so it is the window the mouse is in and gets no WM_MOUSELEAVE */
+    if ((capture = get_capture()))
+    {
+        *hittest = HTCLIENT;
+        *ret_pos = pos;
+        TRACE( "point %s captured by %p\n", wine_dbgstr_point(&pos), capture );
+        return capture;
+    }
     if (tracking->pointer_outside)
     {
         *hittest = HTNOWHERE;
